---
/**
 * /exports/: the sample exports (docs/website.md, "Sample exports"). Real SVG, PNG and draw.io files of the synthetic
 * demo organisations in both themes, the app's renderer's drawing of the views the Export menu offers, made by
 * `node scripts/exports.mjs` with `pnpm render` and published from docs/media/exports/ by the build
 * (src/lib/exports.ts).
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import DemoLink from '../components/DemoLink.astro';
import ExportCard from '../components/ExportCard.astro';
import { sampleExports } from '../lib/exports.js';
import { socialImage } from '../lib/media.js';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/seo.js';
import { repositoryFileUrl } from '../site.js';

const samples = sampleExports();
const meta = {
  title: 'Sample exports',
  description:
    'Download real SVG, PNG and draw.io exports of the gcportrait demo organisations in light and dark, as the app’s renderer draws them.',
  path: '/exports/',
  socialImage: socialImage('exports', 'Sample exports: SVG, PNG and draw.io of the gcportrait demo organisations'),
  jsonLd: [breadcrumbLd([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Sample exports', path: '/exports/' }])],
};
---

<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT -->
<Base meta={meta}>
  <div class="container exports-page">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><span aria-current="page">Sample exports</span></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <h1>Sample exports</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Real SVG, PNG and draw.io files of the synthetic demo organisations, the app’s renderer’s drawing of the views the
      Export menu offers: no real environment is drawn. Each file’s title block names the scope, the lens and the read
      time, then the gcportrait.app tagline; the legend lists what the drawing uses. The non-affiliation statement is in
      the footer below, not in the drawings.
    </p>
    <p>
      Open an SVG to zoom in without losing detail, or download the files to try them in a slide deck, a wiki page or a
      vector editor. The PNGs are drawn at 2×, the Export menu’s default. To export your own views, open the
      <DemoLink>demo</DemoLink> and press Export, or read the <a href="/docs/export/">Export guide</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The SVGs name their fonts, the Roboto stack, without embedding them, as the Export menu writes an SVG unless you
      tick its “Embed fonts” option. Where Roboto is not installed, the viewer draws the labels in another font and they
      may reflow, running a little longer or shorter than in the PNGs, which are always drawn with Roboto.
    </p>
    <p>
      The draw.io files are the same drawings as editable diagrams: zones you can move with what they hold, resources
      with their icons and labels, and lines connected to them, in three layers (the diagram, its connections, the
      title and the legend). “Open in diagrams.net” opens one in a new tab, where diagrams.net loads it from this site;
      or download it and open it in draw.io. Each label names Google Fonts’ stylesheet of Roboto, which diagrams.net
      loads to keep the drawing’s typeface.
    </p>

    <ul class="exports-list" aria-label="Samples">
      {
        samples.map((sample) => (
          <li>
            <ExportCard sample={sample} variant="full" level={2} />
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <section class="exports-how" aria-labelledby="how-made">
      <h2 id="how-made">How they are made</h2>
      <p>
        <code>node scripts/exports.mjs</code> draws each view with <code>pnpm render</code>, the same React components and
        Roboto fonts as the app, rasterised with resvg, and writes the files with a manifest to
        <a href={repositoryFileUrl('docs/media/exports', 'tree')}>docs/media/exports</a> in the repository. The renderer is
        byte-stable: the same command gives the same bytes on every run, which
        <code>node scripts/exports.mjs --check --render</code> verifies. Demo L and XL are left out: L’s overview alone is
        an 8172 × 5284 PNG of about 1.9 MB per theme, which would take the set past its 6 MiB budget.
      </p>
      <p class="muted small">
        Google Cloud and the Google Cloud product icons in these files are trademarks of Google, used unaltered under
        Google’s icon usage terms. When you use a picture, do not present it as Google’s.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .exports-page {
    padding-block: 2rem 1rem;
  }
  .exports-page h1 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  /* The docs pages' breadcrumb (src/layouts/Docs.astro), with the same 44-pixel targets on phones. */
  .breadcrumb ol {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .breadcrumb li + li::before {
    content: '›';
    margin-right: 0.25rem;
  }
  .exports-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  /* A card may be narrower than its longest command line, which scrolls inside its box instead. */
  .exports-list > li {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .exports-how {
    max-width: var(--text-width);
  }
  .small {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 47.99rem) {
    .breadcrumb ol {
      align-items: center;
    }
    .breadcrumb a {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      min-width: 2.75rem;
      min-height: 2.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
